  "domain": "data",
  "definition": "Identity resolution is the process of determining that multiple data records, identifiers, or signals across different systems refer to the same real-world entity \u2014 whether a person, organisation, or device \u2014 and consolidating them into a unified, persistent representation. It combines probabilistic and deterministic matching algorithms, data enrichment, and graph-linking to resolve fragmented identities across first-party, second-party, and third-party data sources.",
